1
00:00:02,202 --> 00:00:04,471
EPISODE 6

2
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:39,740
I'm all done.

3
00:00:43,010 --> 00:00:45,112
She must've been exhausted.

4
00:01:07,634 --> 00:01:10,804
She'll catch a cold sleeping here.

5
00:01:12,272 --> 00:01:14,141
Yun-hui, Yun-hui!

6
00:01:17,544 --> 00:01:19,613
She must be sound asleep.

7
00:01:34,227 --> 00:01:35,696
Ow, my forehead!

8
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:41,068
What's with you?

9
00:01:41,134 --> 00:01:42,836
What did you just do to me?

10
00:01:42,903 --> 00:01:45,639
Um, well, you were sleeping so deeply,

11
00:01:45,706 --> 00:01:47,074
I tried to put you to bed.

12
00:01:47,140 --> 00:01:48,976
Anyway, why are you so heavy?

13
00:01:49,042 --> 00:01:51,578
-You must weigh 70 kg.
-What, you punk?

14
00:01:51,645 --> 00:01:54,081
When did I ever ask you to move me?

15
00:01:54,147 --> 00:01:56,316
Why do things I never asked you to do?

16
00:02:03,323 --> 00:02:04,424
Did you do this too?

17
00:02:04,491 --> 00:02:06,793
I thought you'd be busy in the morning.

18
00:02:06,860 --> 00:02:09,896
Why do you care about that? Why you?

19
00:02:09,963 --> 00:02:11,632
I'm sorry. I'll clear the soju.

20
00:02:11,698 --> 00:02:13,133
Oh, for goodness' sake!

21
00:02:14,101 --> 00:02:17,037
Don't do anything. Leave it.
Just don't do anything!

22
00:02:28,382 --> 00:02:31,118
When will we harvest and tie all this?

23
00:02:32,686 --> 00:02:35,856
I'm dead tired. We're not even slaves.

24
00:02:35,922 --> 00:02:38,225
How long will that guy boss us around?

25
00:02:38,291 --> 00:02:40,427
Quit complaining and get to work.

26
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:42,129
Don't provoke him again.

27
00:02:43,997 --> 00:02:46,667
My, worn out? Eat this corn first.

28
00:02:47,401 --> 00:02:49,603
-Yes!
-Yes! Yes!

29
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:51,004
Corn.

30
00:02:51,938 --> 00:02:53,206
Corn!

31
00:02:58,145 --> 00:02:59,646
Thank you!

32
00:03:02,482 --> 00:03:04,117
Oh, right, ma'am.

33
00:03:04,184 --> 00:03:06,119
Why are you spreading weird rumors?

34
00:03:06,186 --> 00:03:08,555
I told you yesterday was a mix-up.

35
00:03:08,622 --> 00:03:11,525
What? What did I do? I said nothing.

36
00:03:11,591 --> 00:03:14,528
Don't lie. They said you told them.

37
00:03:14,594 --> 00:03:16,630
Gosh, I told them it was a secret.

38
00:03:16,697 --> 00:03:18,532
I can't deal with blabbermouths.

39
00:03:18,598 --> 00:03:22,202
Ma'am, there's really nothing
between me and that woman.

40
00:03:22,269 --> 00:03:24,404
I have high standards, I really do.

41
00:03:24,471 --> 00:03:27,374
I have no interest in a woman
with hair like a ghost.

42
00:03:27,441 --> 00:03:30,677
Besides, am I crazy enough
to like an illegal immigrant?

43
00:03:30,744 --> 00:03:32,312
All right, I get it.

44
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:34,581
Oh, Song Hwa-ran.

45
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,463
She must've heard everything.

46
00:03:49,529 --> 00:03:51,665
Watch what you say to that poor thing.

47
00:03:53,066 --> 00:03:54,868
Uh, well…

48
00:03:54,935 --> 00:03:56,036
Sure, sure, sure.

49
00:03:56,103 --> 00:03:58,371
-You went way too far.
-Watch your mouth.

50
00:03:58,438 --> 00:04:00,774
Karma's going to get you, you punk.

51
00:04:00,841 --> 00:04:01,708
Hurry up.

52
00:04:01,775 --> 00:04:03,977
Okay, I'm coming now.

53
00:04:04,044 --> 00:04:05,679
-I said hurry up!
-I'm coming!

54
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:07,247
He really tried to run off.

55
00:04:11,184 --> 00:04:12,486
All done!

56
00:04:12,552 --> 00:04:17,090
Sir, after all the work we've done,
shouldn't you teach us now?

57
00:04:17,157 --> 00:04:19,392
Sure, I'll start teaching you tomorrow.

58
00:04:19,459 --> 00:04:22,496
But my training is brutal,
so brace yourselves.

59
00:04:22,562 --> 00:04:25,799
Thank you. Thank you so much, sir!

60
00:04:29,936 --> 00:04:31,271
What a relief.

61
00:04:31,338 --> 00:04:34,875
I really thought he wouldn't teach us
after working us to death.

62
00:04:34,941 --> 00:04:37,477
Let's hurry and wash up. I feel gross.

63
00:04:37,544 --> 00:04:40,180
Um, guys, go on ahead.
I have something to do.

64
00:04:40,247 --> 00:04:41,448
Something to do? What?

65
00:04:41,515 --> 00:04:44,818
Well, uh, it's just something.
Anyway, see you later.

66
00:04:45,685 --> 00:04:47,587
Jeez, he's acting shady.

67
00:04:51,358 --> 00:04:54,060
Um, excuse me, Hwa-ran.

68
00:04:55,362 --> 00:04:56,997
What do you want?

69
00:04:57,063 --> 00:04:59,466
What I said earlier was too harsh.

70
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,168
I'm sorry.

71
00:05:01,835 --> 00:05:03,336
There is no need.

72
00:05:03,403 --> 00:05:05,071
Just leave.

73
00:05:06,606 --> 00:05:08,809
I lost it because of you.

74
00:05:08,875 --> 00:05:10,477
Hey.

75
00:05:10,544 --> 00:05:13,246
Isn't it common courtesy
to accept an apology?

76
00:05:14,514 --> 00:05:15,949
Forget it.

77
00:05:16,016 --> 00:05:19,820
Why would you care about
an illegal immigrant like me?

78
00:05:20,620 --> 00:05:21,621
Look here!

79
00:05:21,688 --> 00:05:24,858
Look at me and answer
when I'm talking to you!

80
00:05:24,925 --> 00:05:26,259
I said forget it!

81
00:05:36,036 --> 00:05:37,804
S-s-s-snake…

82
00:05:39,873 --> 00:05:42,409
Stay still, stay still, stay still.

83
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:47,881
Are you all right?

84
00:05:47,948 --> 00:05:49,115
I think it's a viper.

85
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:51,284
Let me see. Where did it bite you?

86
00:05:51,351 --> 00:05:53,320
My lip, my lip.

87
00:05:53,386 --> 00:05:56,089
-Quick, call 119.
-There is no time for that.

88
00:05:56,156 --> 00:05:57,357
Then what do we do?

89
00:05:57,424 --> 00:05:59,526
What else? I must suck out the venom.

90
00:05:59,593 --> 00:06:01,828
Suck it out? How?

91
00:06:01,895 --> 00:06:03,663
Hold still, all right?

92
00:06:06,399 --> 00:06:08,134
Wait, this isn't right, though.

93
00:06:08,201 --> 00:06:10,303
Still, this just isn't right.

94
00:06:17,210 --> 00:06:20,080
Ma'am, it's not what it looks like.

95
00:06:20,146 --> 00:06:22,315
-Don't move.
-Wait, hold on.

96
00:06:22,382 --> 00:06:24,351
Go on, finish what you were doing.

97
00:06:24,417 --> 00:06:26,519
I'll pretend I saw nothing, so go on.

98
00:06:26,586 --> 00:06:27,988
Wait a second.

99
00:06:28,655 --> 00:06:30,290
Don't move.

100
00:06:30,357 --> 00:06:31,691
It's not like that.

101
00:06:31,758 --> 00:06:33,994
Should we get spicy rice cakes today?

102
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,128
Okay, sure.

103
00:06:35,195 --> 00:06:37,998
Hey, isn't that the kid with no dad?

104
00:06:38,064 --> 00:06:39,266
Should I hit him?

105
00:06:39,332 --> 00:06:40,367
-Sure!

106
00:06:46,806 --> 00:06:49,309
You blocked my way!

107
00:06:49,376 --> 00:06:53,246
If you're mad, go tell your dad.

108
00:06:53,313 --> 00:06:56,917
Oh, right, you don't even know
who your dad is, do you?

109
00:07:06,459 --> 00:07:09,963
Does Su-yeon really have a boyfriend?

110
00:07:10,030 --> 00:07:12,832
Hey, do you only think
about that woman all day?

111
00:07:12,899 --> 00:07:15,902
Are you possessed
by a love-starved ghost or what?

112
00:07:16,603 --> 00:07:20,640
I told you, I have unavoidable reasons.

113
00:07:20,707 --> 00:07:23,243
I don't have time. I'm out of time.

114
00:07:23,910 --> 00:07:27,213
Do you guys have any idea how I feel?

115
00:07:28,515 --> 00:07:31,217
Hey, don't sulk.

116
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:34,220
I still don't get it.
Why don't we have time?

117
00:07:34,287 --> 00:07:35,588
I don't know.

118
00:07:40,293 --> 00:07:41,361
-Hey.
-What?

119
00:07:41,428 --> 00:07:43,697
I need to stop somewhere, so go ahead.

120
00:07:43,763 --> 00:07:45,432
Where?

121
00:07:47,734 --> 00:07:49,703
Hey, rock star.

122
00:07:58,144 --> 00:08:00,013
Why are you such a mess?

123
00:08:00,947 --> 00:08:02,682
You got picked on again.

124
00:08:03,883 --> 00:08:06,086
It's because you always put up with it.

125
00:08:06,152 --> 00:08:08,121
You have to fight back to stop them.

126
00:08:08,188 --> 00:08:10,423
Mom said not to fight.

127
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:13,827
She told me I can't let people
call me a fatherless kid.

128
00:08:13,893 --> 00:08:15,462
She said to always hold it in.

129
00:08:16,596 --> 00:08:18,598
Even so, that's too much.

130
00:08:19,733 --> 00:08:22,102
So you'll live like this every day?
Forever?

131
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:25,505
But Wang-bae is big and really strong.

132
00:08:26,639 --> 00:08:30,176
Don't worry about that, kid.

133
00:08:30,243 --> 00:08:33,813
Wang-bae or Wrong-bae,
your big bro is on it.

134
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:34,781
I'll handle him.

135
00:08:34,848 --> 00:08:36,783
Follow me.

136
00:08:47,293 --> 00:08:49,796
-Go away!
-So that's Wang-bae.

137
00:08:50,563 --> 00:08:51,631
-Go away!
-You going?

138
00:08:51,698 --> 00:08:53,767
Go do what I told you and come back.

139
00:08:53,833 --> 00:08:55,068
Hurry, go on.

140
00:08:55,869 --> 00:08:57,704
Go! Go!

141
00:08:58,671 --> 00:09:01,074
Go! Go away!

142
00:09:03,443 --> 00:09:04,444
What was that?

143
00:09:13,820 --> 00:09:16,089
Gosh, I'm exhausted.

144
00:09:16,856 --> 00:09:18,024
You're back?

145
00:09:18,091 --> 00:09:19,292
Is your forehead okay?

146
00:09:19,359 --> 00:09:20,894
It hurts like crazy, jeez.

147
00:09:21,561 --> 00:09:23,196
But why are you alone again?

148
00:09:23,263 --> 00:09:25,165
I don't know.

149
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:27,367
Everyone has such pressing affairs.

150
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:31,838
Hey, what happened to your lip?

151
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:34,207
Don't ask me anything.

152
00:09:34,274 --> 00:09:35,375
Oh, that's right.

153
00:09:35,442 --> 00:09:37,110
I heard you kissed Hwa-ran?

154
00:09:37,177 --> 00:09:39,446
What? How did you know…

155
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:43,616
I bet it's that lady again…

156
00:09:43,683 --> 00:09:45,185
You really kissed Hwa-ran…

157
00:09:45,251 --> 00:09:47,921
I can't believe you denied it so hard!

158
00:09:48,855 --> 00:09:50,090
Fine.

159
00:09:50,156 --> 00:09:52,826
Think whatever you want, whatever!

160
00:09:52,892 --> 00:09:54,594
I'm dating and marrying Hwa-ran!

161
00:09:54,661 --> 00:09:56,996
I'll live happily in Yanbian. Happy?

162
00:09:57,063 --> 00:09:58,598
-Really? Congrats!
-Sure!

163
00:09:58,665 --> 00:10:00,400
What a brazen little punk.

164
00:10:00,467 --> 00:10:02,969
Kids these days really move fast.

165
00:10:03,036 --> 00:10:03,903
Right?

166
00:10:04,671 --> 00:10:06,306
Oh, gosh, that's right.

167
00:10:06,372 --> 00:10:08,741
Min-ho's running late, though. Gosh.

168
00:10:10,777 --> 00:10:12,312
Seen my boxing gloves, Sis?

169
00:10:12,378 --> 00:10:14,214
No, I haven't. Why? Are they gone?

170
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:16,683
Weird. I wanted to work out for once.

171
00:10:16,749 --> 00:10:17,884
Where did they go?

172
00:10:21,955 --> 00:10:23,690
Begin!

173
00:10:23,756 --> 00:10:26,226
Get him! Get him!

174
00:10:26,292 --> 00:10:29,929
Get him! Get him! Get him!

175
00:10:29,996 --> 00:10:33,500
Get him! Get him! Get him! Get him!

176
00:10:33,566 --> 00:10:37,971
Get him! Get him! Get him! Get him!

177
00:10:38,738 --> 00:10:40,707
Min-ho, you have to dodge!

178
00:10:41,407 --> 00:10:43,042
Why are you taking every hit?

179
00:10:43,109 --> 00:10:45,612
This won't do. Use the secret weapon!

180
00:10:45,678 --> 00:10:46,813
Now! Right now!

181
00:10:48,248 --> 00:10:51,951
Get him! Get him! Get him!

182
00:10:55,455 --> 00:10:58,024
-It hurts!
-Wang-bae, are you okay? You okay?

183
00:11:02,328 --> 00:11:05,765
Min-ho didn't hold back
because he's a bad fighter.

184
00:11:05,832 --> 00:11:07,934
He just didn't want to fight a friend.

185
00:11:08,601 --> 00:11:12,038
Wang-bae, you're his precious friend.

186
00:11:12,105 --> 00:11:14,607
Now, shake hands and make up!

187
00:11:15,108 --> 00:11:17,076
-Let's be friends.
-Okay.

188
00:11:17,143 --> 00:11:18,411
-No more fighting.
-Okay.

189
00:11:18,478 --> 00:11:21,080
-Goodbye, sir.
-Get home safe.

190
00:11:22,248 --> 00:11:24,450
Min-ho, let's take off the gloves.

191
00:11:28,922 --> 00:11:31,057
But isn't this playing dirty?

192
00:11:31,124 --> 00:11:33,426
It's fine if you don't get caught, kid.

193
00:11:33,493 --> 00:11:37,130
Keep it a total secret from your mom.

194
00:11:38,431 --> 00:11:40,066
Let's go.

195
00:11:43,469 --> 00:11:46,306
Why is Min-ho so late?
I can't reach him by phone.

196
00:11:47,173 --> 00:11:48,274
Mom!

197
00:11:49,609 --> 00:11:51,978
Gosh, Min-ho, why are you so late?

198
00:11:53,513 --> 00:11:54,714
What's with your face?

199
00:11:54,781 --> 00:11:56,683
That's nothing at all.

200
00:11:56,749 --> 00:12:00,153
Call it a badge of honor
from a duel between real men?

201
00:12:00,220 --> 00:12:02,388
-A duel?
-You know that kid.

202
00:12:02,455 --> 00:12:04,490
Wang-bae, who always bullied Min-ho?

203
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:06,259
Right? Isn't that right?

204
00:12:06,326 --> 00:12:08,928
He took him on today, man to man,

205
00:12:08,995 --> 00:12:11,097
and they fought fair and square.

206
00:12:11,164 --> 00:12:14,634
Then Min-ho got him! Bam, one punch!

207
00:12:14,701 --> 00:12:15,702
-Right?
-Yes.

208
00:12:16,369 --> 00:12:17,537
Min-ho, in your room.

209
00:12:24,811 --> 00:12:26,212
Just what are you doing?

210
00:12:28,481 --> 00:12:31,084
-What did I do?
-First it was the talent show.

211
00:12:31,150 --> 00:12:32,585
Now you made him brawl?

212
00:12:32,652 --> 00:12:35,121
You just let him keep getting bullied?

213
00:12:35,188 --> 00:12:36,889
He can just put up with it!

214
00:12:38,391 --> 00:12:39,726
You know you're weird?

215
00:12:39,792 --> 00:12:43,229
If your kid is getting bullied,

216
00:12:43,296 --> 00:12:46,332
shouldn't a mom run over
and yank his hair out?

217
00:12:46,399 --> 00:12:50,837
Or tell him, "Don't put up with it.
Go beat him up too!"

218
00:12:50,903 --> 00:12:52,572
Isn't that what a mom says?

219
00:12:52,639 --> 00:12:54,741
What if he's called fatherless again?

220
00:12:55,475 --> 00:12:57,543
Or say he's just a single mom's son?

221
00:12:58,344 --> 00:13:00,947
You think staying quiet is easy for me?

222
00:13:01,014 --> 00:13:02,582
I'm doing it all for Min-ho.

223
00:13:02,649 --> 00:13:04,384
For Min-ho?

224
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:07,086
And not for yourself?

225
00:13:07,153 --> 00:13:08,021
What?

226
00:13:08,087 --> 00:13:11,858
You're just worried
people will point fingers at you.

227
00:13:12,425 --> 00:13:14,394
Is it Min-ho's fault he has no dad?

228
00:13:15,161 --> 00:13:16,596
It's not Min-ho's fault.

229
00:13:17,330 --> 00:13:18,698
Then again…

230
00:13:19,699 --> 00:13:21,701
my mom also brushed it all aside

231
00:13:22,602 --> 00:13:24,137
and made me apologize first

232
00:13:24,203 --> 00:13:27,040
without asking what happened or why.

233
00:13:27,106 --> 00:13:28,775
Always, "It's my fault."

234
00:13:28,841 --> 00:13:31,477
"I will never do it again.
Please forgive me."

235
00:13:31,544 --> 00:13:32,612
He has no dad.

236
00:13:32,679 --> 00:13:34,480
Even his mom isn't on his side.

237
00:13:35,715 --> 00:13:36,883
Who has Min-ho's back?

238
00:13:37,884 --> 00:13:40,653
Min-ho is still just a little kid.

239
00:13:41,187 --> 00:13:44,057
Min-ho shouldn't learn
to just put up with it now.

240
00:13:44,123 --> 00:13:47,060
"My mom really is on my side."

241
00:13:47,126 --> 00:13:49,462
"Whatever I do, she'll protect me."

242
00:13:49,529 --> 00:13:51,964
That's what you need to make him feel.

243
00:13:52,031 --> 00:13:53,299
Understand?

244
00:14:17,690 --> 00:14:21,461
Mom, I'm sorry. I won't fight again.

245
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:31,738
Want to use my arm as a pillow?

246
00:14:31,804 --> 00:14:33,206
Huh?

247
00:14:33,272 --> 00:14:34,507
Yes.

248
00:14:37,377 --> 00:14:41,647
Come here, my baby. Oh, my sweet boy.

249
00:14:44,083 --> 00:14:45,885
Does it hurt right here?

250
00:14:45,952 --> 00:14:48,521
I'm okay. Min-gi put medicine on it.

251
00:14:48,588 --> 00:14:50,723
Seems you got really close to Min-gi.

252
00:14:50,790 --> 00:14:52,725
Yes, Min-gi is super cool.

253
00:14:52,792 --> 00:14:54,293
He's smart, and he's funny.

254
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:57,830
Gosh, you're his biggest fan,
you really are his number-one fan.

255
00:14:57,897 --> 00:14:58,831
Like him so much?

256
00:14:58,898 --> 00:15:01,234
Yes, Min-gi seems like a good person.

257
00:15:03,069 --> 00:15:06,272
Right, he's not a bad guy.

258
00:15:08,040 --> 00:15:10,243
But Min-ho, how did you win?

259
00:15:10,309 --> 00:15:11,911
Wang-bae is really strong.

260
00:15:11,978 --> 00:15:15,281
Min-gi taught me a secret weapon.

261
00:15:15,348 --> 00:15:17,116
A secret weapon?

262
00:15:17,183 --> 00:15:19,485
This is a secret, though.

263
00:15:26,392 --> 00:15:29,128
What? He made you hit him
with a rock in your hand?

264
00:15:29,195 --> 00:15:31,297
He said it's fine if you're not caught.

265
00:15:32,965 --> 00:15:35,334
That rotten bastard, seriously!

266
00:15:44,310 --> 00:15:47,246
Hey! Lee Min-gi!

267
00:16:25,551 --> 00:16:28,254
Hmm… Not bad at all.

268
00:16:28,321 --> 00:16:30,823
You made these field ridges real nice.

269
00:16:32,058 --> 00:16:34,961
Now, shall I check the soil quality?

270
00:16:41,801 --> 00:16:43,870
Oh my god, what did he just eat?

271
00:16:46,239 --> 00:16:48,274
Nutrient levels are satisfactory too.

272
00:16:49,775 --> 00:16:51,444
That'll do.

273
00:16:52,345 --> 00:16:55,181
But why didn't you put
plastic mulch on the ridges?

274
00:16:55,715 --> 00:16:58,251
Without plastic,
the weeds will give you hell.

275
00:16:58,317 --> 00:17:01,187
Weeds are no big deal.
We can just pull them out.

276
00:17:01,254 --> 00:17:03,122
You clueless, reckless fools.

277
00:17:03,189 --> 00:17:06,092
Pull them, turn around,
and weeds grow right back.

278
00:17:06,158 --> 00:17:08,027
Even if a dust-sized root is left,

279
00:17:08,094 --> 00:17:10,496
weeds will spread in every direction.

280
00:17:10,563 --> 00:17:12,832
With four of us, we'll manage somehow.

281
00:17:12,899 --> 00:17:17,270
Admiral Yi Sun-sin stopped invaders,
but even he couldn't stop the weeds.

282
00:17:17,336 --> 00:17:21,140
Even if you still had 12 hoes,
it'd be impossible, you punks!

283
00:17:21,207 --> 00:17:23,976
We just have no money,
no money to buy the plastic.

284
00:17:24,644 --> 00:17:26,946
Sir, we'll handle the weeds for now.

285
00:17:27,013 --> 00:17:28,381
Let's start the seedlings.

286
00:17:28,447 --> 00:17:30,149
Do we just sow the seeds first?

287
00:17:30,783 --> 00:17:33,519
Freeze! What are you doing right now?

288
00:17:33,586 --> 00:17:36,055
You're starting seedlings right here?

289
00:17:36,122 --> 00:17:38,090
-In the open field?
-Yes, why?

290
00:17:38,958 --> 00:17:42,595
Hey, you punk.
Seedlings are newborns, newborns!

291
00:17:42,662 --> 00:17:45,865
What would happen if you left
a newborn out on the street?

292
00:17:45,932 --> 00:17:48,668
If it's a bit too hot,
they burn to death.

293
00:17:48,734 --> 00:17:51,304
If it's a bit too cold,
they freeze to death.

294
00:17:51,370 --> 00:17:53,973
-Then what should we do?
-What do you think?

295
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:57,944
You start seedlings in a greenhouse,
cozy as a mother's arms.

296
00:17:58,010 --> 00:18:01,213
We don't have a greenhouse.
Can't we just give it a try?

297
00:18:01,280 --> 00:18:02,882
Absolutely not!

298
00:18:02,949 --> 00:18:06,852
It's none of my business
whether you ruin your crops or not.

299
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:09,255
But if you fail,

300
00:18:09,322 --> 00:18:13,392
it'll tarnish my reputation
as the village's Farming God.

301
00:18:13,459 --> 00:18:17,163
Want to learn cabbage farming?
Get a greenhouse first, then come back.

302
00:18:17,830 --> 00:18:20,166
Sir, it's fine. It's fine.

303
00:18:20,232 --> 00:18:21,767
Uh, we can just try first.

304
00:18:21,834 --> 00:18:23,769
Let go of me. Let go.

305
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:29,342
Urgent! Residents of Hadurok-ri.

306
00:18:29,408 --> 00:18:31,243
Please hurry to the village hall.

307
00:18:31,310 --> 00:18:32,445
Village Head Yun-hui

308
00:18:32,511 --> 00:18:35,448
Did something happen?
Why the sudden village meeting?

309
00:18:35,514 --> 00:18:38,751
Wow, do those come by text these days?

310
00:18:38,818 --> 00:18:40,453
Don't they use loudspeakers?

311
00:18:40,519 --> 00:18:42,655
-Dear Village Heads.
-It's "villagers."

312
00:18:42,722 --> 00:18:45,891
You're talking like it's the Stone Age.

313
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:47,960
Are you filming Hometown Report?

314
00:18:48,027 --> 00:18:49,662
We use it all too, you punk.

315
00:18:49,729 --> 00:18:53,299
Texts, messengers, social media, blogs.

316
00:18:53,366 --> 00:18:56,335
Plus, with the tearoom girls in town,

317
00:18:56,402 --> 00:18:58,304
I even have a group chat, you punks.

318
00:18:58,371 --> 00:18:59,772
With the tearoom girls?

319
00:19:03,409 --> 00:19:05,711
This is definitely no ordinary matter.

320
00:19:05,778 --> 00:19:07,713
Let's hurry over there.

321
00:19:07,780 --> 00:19:09,215
So what's going on?

322
00:19:09,281 --> 00:19:11,250
Please wait a bit. They're coming.

323
00:19:12,918 --> 00:19:14,220
What's going on?

324
00:19:14,286 --> 00:19:16,689
Oh, just wait and see. It's good news.

325
00:19:16,756 --> 00:19:18,090
Is that so?

326
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:20,326
Good grief, I was giving a lecture.

327
00:19:20,393 --> 00:19:22,762
What's going on? Why order me around?

328
00:19:22,828 --> 00:19:24,830
Please hurry and sit. Just sit down.

329
00:19:24,897 --> 00:19:26,999
Have a seat. Come on, sit down quick.

330
00:19:27,800 --> 00:19:29,735
Yes, come on in.

331
00:19:29,802 --> 00:19:32,705
Don't be shocked, everyone. Listen up.

332
00:19:32,772 --> 00:19:35,307
For Sunday, which means tomorrow,

333
00:19:35,374 --> 00:19:38,844
Sang-deuk's blind date
has finally been scheduled!

334
00:19:38,911 --> 00:19:40,079
Oh, thank goodness!

335
00:19:43,349 --> 00:19:46,519
What is this?
You called us just for a blind date?

336
00:19:46,585 --> 00:19:49,422
Is this really big enough
to hold a village meeting?

337
00:19:49,488 --> 00:19:50,823
Of course it is!

338
00:19:50,890 --> 00:19:53,559
Sang-deuk is the last bachelor
in our village.

339
00:19:53,626 --> 00:19:56,796
Let me briefly introduce
the woman's profile first.

340
00:19:56,862 --> 00:19:59,098
She is 32 years old,

341
00:19:59,165 --> 00:20:01,834
studied early childhood education
at a Seoul college

342
00:20:01,901 --> 00:20:04,170
and graduated with top marks, they say.

343
00:20:04,236 --> 00:20:06,572
-Oh, that's great!
-Well done!

344
00:20:08,040 --> 00:20:09,375
Stop it already.

345
00:20:09,442 --> 00:20:12,511
Is a woman like her crazy enough
to marry into the sticks?

346
00:20:12,578 --> 00:20:14,146
I heard she likes rural life.

347
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:16,348
That makes it even more dangerous.

348
00:20:16,415 --> 00:20:18,217
What woman is like that nowadays?

349
00:20:18,884 --> 00:20:19,985
She's a gold digger,

350
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:23,255
or she definitely has a major flaw.
Forget it.

351
00:20:23,322 --> 00:20:25,825
Hey, at least look at her photo.

352
00:20:25,891 --> 00:20:27,893
Come on, I already said forget it.

353
00:20:30,696 --> 00:20:32,198
I'll at least meet her.

354
00:20:35,868 --> 00:20:39,271
Now, I'm taking sponsorships
for Sang-deuk's matchmaking date.

355
00:20:39,338 --> 00:20:41,674
A car, a watch, socks, a suit.

356
00:20:41,741 --> 00:20:43,209
Anyway, whatever it may be,

357
00:20:43,275 --> 00:20:45,010
if it's nice, please sponsor us.

358
00:20:45,077 --> 00:20:48,447
Sponsorships? What's the point of that?

359
00:20:48,514 --> 00:20:51,183
He needs actual skill with women.

360
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,018
In Vietnam and Uzbekistan
Sang-deuk

361
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:54,286
got dumped every time.

362
00:20:54,353 --> 00:20:56,055
Keep quiet!

363
00:20:56,822 --> 00:21:00,993
Ma'am, your talent for rubbing salt
in people's wounds for a laugh

364
00:21:01,060 --> 00:21:03,129
is truly worthy of the national team.

365
00:21:03,195 --> 00:21:04,363
By the way, though,

366
00:21:04,430 --> 00:21:06,298
Seoul women are so picky,

367
00:21:06,365 --> 00:21:08,534
winning her over won't be easy at all.

368
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:10,803
Oh, don't worry about that.

369
00:21:10,870 --> 00:21:12,338
We've got guys from Seoul.

370
00:21:12,404 --> 00:21:15,541
Right! We have these fine
Seoul bachelors right here.

371
00:21:15,608 --> 00:21:18,010
Let me ask you for a favor, okay?

372
00:21:18,077 --> 00:21:20,513
But what could we possibly do to help?

373
00:21:20,579 --> 00:21:23,783
It's not just a casual blind date.
It's a matchmaking date.

374
00:21:23,849 --> 00:21:26,852
It's an impossible game to begin with.

375
00:21:26,919 --> 00:21:28,187
She's in another league.

376
00:21:33,425 --> 00:21:35,728
No, it's a doomed game from the start.

377
00:21:35,795 --> 00:21:37,596
No way, no way. This won't work.

378
00:21:37,663 --> 00:21:39,031
Wait, look--

379
00:21:39,098 --> 00:21:41,500
You little bastards!
What's wrong with me?

380
00:21:41,567 --> 00:21:44,603
I heard you boys need a greenhouse.

381
00:21:50,709 --> 00:21:52,578
So you'll lend us this greenhouse?

382
00:21:52,645 --> 00:21:54,680
And for free, at that.

383
00:21:54,747 --> 00:21:58,184
Ma'am, didn't you say you'd plant
strawberries here this winter?

384
00:21:58,250 --> 00:22:00,419
Does a measly strawberry patch matter?

385
00:22:00,486 --> 00:22:02,888
If I can just marry off Sang-deuk,

386
00:22:02,955 --> 00:22:04,990
what wouldn't I do?

387
00:22:05,057 --> 00:22:07,960
If the match fails,
you all know what happens, right?

388
00:22:10,596 --> 00:22:13,833
Please do not worry about that at all.

389
00:22:13,899 --> 00:22:17,536
This guy's nickname is
the Hongdae Sticky Rice Cake.

390
00:22:17,603 --> 00:22:19,138
Now, why Sticky Rice Cake?

391
00:22:19,205 --> 00:22:22,241
His silver tongue is so chewy,
the ladies just

392
00:22:22,308 --> 00:22:24,210
stick to him like sticky rice.

393
00:22:25,344 --> 00:22:28,914
And this guy needs no description.

394
00:22:28,981 --> 00:22:31,050
Samcheong-dong One Shot, One Kill.

395
00:22:33,085 --> 00:22:35,154
And this is our youngest, Ki-jun.

396
00:22:35,221 --> 00:22:37,957
Even while studying
for the civil service exam,

397
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:40,359
he seduced a rice-bowl stand worker

398
00:22:40,426 --> 00:22:43,128
and lived on rice bowls
for all three daily meals.

399
00:22:43,195 --> 00:22:44,496
Don Juan of Noryangjin.

400
00:22:45,431 --> 00:22:48,601
So please trust us
and leave it in our hands.

401
00:22:48,667 --> 00:22:50,035
Right, guys?

402
00:22:56,242 --> 00:22:57,910
I'm back.

403
00:22:59,478 --> 00:23:01,347
Ramen again?

404
00:23:02,414 --> 00:23:04,483
Is this house a ramen ambassador?

405
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:06,619
Hurry and eat before it gets soggy.

406
00:23:07,186 --> 00:23:09,321
Soon, the day ramen makes you happiest

407
00:23:09,388 --> 00:23:10,489
will come for you.

408
00:23:10,556 --> 00:23:13,158
What a joke.
It's a waste of food money, jeez.

409
00:23:16,362 --> 00:23:19,632
Hey, little rock star.
What are you doing?

410
00:23:29,041 --> 00:23:30,242
DRAWING HOMEWORK

411
00:23:30,309 --> 00:23:31,710
What are you doing now?

412
00:23:31,777 --> 00:23:33,712
Just say it. Why write it down?

413
00:23:33,779 --> 00:23:36,181
You taught a kid
to hit people with a rock.

414
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:37,283
Anything to say?

415
00:23:37,349 --> 00:23:39,752
You're banned from approaching Min-ho.

416
00:23:39,818 --> 00:23:41,921
Don't come within ten meters, got it?

417
00:23:41,987 --> 00:23:45,357
Oh, really?
Why not put an ankle monitor on me?

418
00:23:45,424 --> 00:23:47,593
An ankle monitor? That's a good idea.

419
00:23:47,660 --> 00:23:49,194
Can I just buy that online?

420
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:50,896
Oh, seriously.

421
00:23:57,269 --> 00:23:58,637
Any left for me?

422
00:24:00,739 --> 00:24:04,076
What kind of woman uses a rubber band?

423
00:24:04,143 --> 00:24:05,611
Don't you have a hairpin?

424
00:24:05,678 --> 00:24:07,546
I'd need at least one real man here

425
00:24:07,613 --> 00:24:09,982
to wear a hairpin or headband, right?

426
00:24:10,049 --> 00:24:11,917
Who'd I wear a hairpin to impress?

427
00:24:11,984 --> 00:24:13,485
Hey, hurry up and eat.

428
00:24:13,552 --> 00:24:15,654
We have to coach Sang-deuk on his date.

429
00:24:24,196 --> 00:24:27,700
Sang-deuk,
what kind of dramas do you like?

430
00:24:28,901 --> 00:24:30,536
I don't watch TV.

431
00:24:31,537 --> 00:24:33,772
Oh, I see.

432
00:24:35,140 --> 00:24:39,044
Then what kind of sports do you like?

433
00:24:39,111 --> 00:24:40,079
Shoveling.

434
00:24:41,413 --> 00:24:42,948
Oh…

435
00:24:43,015 --> 00:24:46,318
So what are your hobbies?

436
00:24:46,385 --> 00:24:47,252
Shoveling.

437
00:24:48,887 --> 00:24:52,791
What do you do when you meet friends?

438
00:24:52,858 --> 00:24:54,693
Shoveling.

439
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:55,694
Damn it!

440
00:24:55,761 --> 00:24:57,763
Seriously, please just stop.

441
00:24:57,830 --> 00:25:00,699
Sir, is "shoveling" all you can say?

442
00:25:00,766 --> 00:25:02,601
I just answered honestly.

443
00:25:02,668 --> 00:25:05,637
And sir, when underwear
gets stuck to your butt,

444
00:25:05,704 --> 00:25:07,773
why peel it off? It's not a sticker.

445
00:25:07,840 --> 00:25:10,576
When underwear sticks to my butt,
I peel it off.

446
00:25:10,642 --> 00:25:12,011
Should I just leave it?

447
00:25:12,978 --> 00:25:15,848
Then will you peel it off
even in front of a woman?

448
00:25:16,448 --> 00:25:20,252
I won't leave my underwear
stuck to my butt with a woman there

449
00:25:20,319 --> 00:25:23,088
and peel it off when she's gone.
I'm no coward.

450
00:25:24,156 --> 00:25:25,190
What do you mean?

451
00:25:25,257 --> 00:25:27,026
No, this won't work. Not at all.

452
00:25:27,092 --> 00:25:29,995
This was a lost cause from the start.

453
00:25:30,062 --> 00:25:32,798
You're not just a bomb,
you're a nuclear bomb.

454
00:25:32,865 --> 00:25:34,366
You're even worse than me.

455
00:25:42,674 --> 00:25:44,343
My goodness, who is this?

456
00:25:45,878 --> 00:25:48,414
You always look like a mountain bandit.

457
00:25:48,480 --> 00:25:51,550
But dressed up, you look pretty good.

458
00:25:51,617 --> 00:25:52,918
Come on, stop it.

459
00:25:52,985 --> 00:25:54,953
I just don't usually dress up.

460
00:25:55,020 --> 00:25:56,855
My base face is pure Won Bin.

461
00:25:58,057 --> 00:26:01,827
You boys worked so hard.
Thank you so much.

462
00:26:03,262 --> 00:26:05,697
It wasn't all that easy, though.

463
00:26:05,764 --> 00:26:08,700
In the spirit of creating
something out of nothing,

464
00:26:08,767 --> 00:26:11,904
this is merely the result
of doing my utmost.

465
00:26:13,772 --> 00:26:16,241
Hey, Sang-deuk, you rascal.

466
00:26:16,308 --> 00:26:18,377
You have to succeed this time.

467
00:26:18,444 --> 00:26:21,880
Let me finally enjoy a meal
cooked by a daughter-in-law.

468
00:26:21,947 --> 00:26:24,349
Gosh, I told you not to worry.

469
00:26:24,416 --> 00:26:25,651
I'll be off, then.

470
00:26:25,717 --> 00:26:27,286
-Okay, do well.
-Go for it!

471
00:26:27,352 --> 00:26:29,021
-Good luck!
-Be sure to succeed!

472
00:26:29,088 --> 00:26:29,955
You can do it!

473
00:26:36,028 --> 00:26:37,629
You all worked hard.

474
00:26:37,696 --> 00:26:40,132
-Oh, thank you.
-Want some of these?

475
00:26:41,333 --> 00:26:42,901
Thank you, sir!

476
00:26:45,204 --> 00:26:47,873
Grandpa, do you farm almonds too?

477
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:51,910
No, I love these chocolate bars.

478
00:26:52,578 --> 00:26:53,846
But my teeth are bad,

479
00:26:55,981 --> 00:26:59,084
so I just can't chew the almonds.

480
00:27:02,988 --> 00:27:03,989
Want some more?

481
00:27:06,992 --> 00:27:08,627
No, we don't want any!

482
00:27:12,297 --> 00:27:14,433
-Where's the place?
-You're here, sir?

483
00:27:14,500 --> 00:27:17,202
Just head all the way inside there.

484
00:27:17,269 --> 00:27:18,704
-Inside there?
-Yes.

485
00:27:20,439 --> 00:27:22,608
Hey, move the truck.

486
00:27:22,674 --> 00:27:25,144
I'm sorry, I'll move right away.

487
00:27:27,079 --> 00:27:29,181
Mi-yeong?

488
00:27:30,649 --> 00:27:32,284
Sang-deuk?

489
00:27:38,257 --> 00:27:40,826
-Your daughter?
-Yes.

490
00:27:41,593 --> 00:27:43,929
She's whined all day
to go back to Seoul.

491
00:27:45,531 --> 00:27:48,400
It's been so long. How have you been?

492
00:27:49,201 --> 00:27:50,869
Just getting by.

493
00:27:50,936 --> 00:27:53,505
Anyway, why did you come back to town?

494
00:27:54,139 --> 00:27:57,142
I was crazy busy with my business,

495
00:27:57,876 --> 00:28:00,679
but Dad kept begging
to go back to his hometown.

496
00:28:00,746 --> 00:28:03,682
-I wrapped things up and came.
-Your father came too?

497
00:28:03,749 --> 00:28:05,384
I should at least say hello.

498
00:28:05,450 --> 00:28:06,518
Forget it.

499
00:28:06,585 --> 00:28:08,687
He won't even recognize you.

500
00:28:09,288 --> 00:28:10,923
He has severe dementia.

501
00:28:10,989 --> 00:28:12,558
Dementia?

502
00:28:13,158 --> 00:28:14,927
Oh, goodness.

503
00:28:15,961 --> 00:28:18,463
Then did your husband come down too?

504
00:28:19,331 --> 00:28:22,234
No, I got divorced two years ago.

505
00:28:23,302 --> 00:28:25,270
-Divorced?
-Yes.

506
00:28:26,038 --> 00:28:28,740
But you're married, right? Any kids?

507
00:28:29,508 --> 00:28:33,212
Yes, well, you see…

508
00:28:33,912 --> 00:28:37,182
Sang-deuk,
what are you still doing here?

509
00:28:37,249 --> 00:28:38,850
Wait, you… You…

510
00:28:39,718 --> 00:28:41,119
Aren't you Mi-yeong?

511
00:28:41,954 --> 00:28:44,656
It's been so long, ma'am.
How have you been?

512
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:46,024
Why are you here?

513
00:28:46,091 --> 00:28:48,060
She says her dad's sick, so she came.

514
00:28:48,126 --> 00:28:50,062
What nerve do you have coming here?

515
00:28:50,128 --> 00:28:53,098
How can you come here and face me?

516
00:28:53,165 --> 00:28:54,132
Please stop, Mom.

517
00:28:54,199 --> 00:28:55,901
You spineless fool!

518
00:28:55,968 --> 00:28:57,369
You were so humiliated,

519
00:28:57,436 --> 00:28:59,972
and you're flirting with this girl?

520
00:29:00,038 --> 00:29:02,874
What are you doing here?
You'll miss your blind date!

521
00:29:03,542 --> 00:29:06,778
Blind date? You're still not married?

522
00:29:06,845 --> 00:29:09,815
Yes, he's still single because of you.

523
00:29:09,881 --> 00:29:11,617
What, are you gloating?

524
00:29:11,683 --> 00:29:14,286
I told you to stop.
Why embarrass me like this?

525
00:29:14,353 --> 00:29:17,389
Let's go, hurry. Come on, hurry.

526
00:29:17,456 --> 00:29:19,091
Goodbye, ma'am.

527
00:29:20,259 --> 00:29:22,427
What was that?

528
00:29:22,494 --> 00:29:23,929
Go, or the geezer snaps!

529
00:29:23,996 --> 00:29:25,364
-The geezer?
-Right, right.

530
00:29:25,430 --> 00:29:27,699
-Call him "sir."
-If the elder gets mad…

531
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:30,035
Don't do that.

532
00:29:31,737 --> 00:29:33,372
No, no, no, no, no!

533
00:29:33,438 --> 00:29:35,607
-Were you having fun with Grandpa?
-Yes.

534
00:29:38,977 --> 00:29:41,280
Dad, is it nice being in your hometown?

535
00:29:45,150 --> 00:29:46,752
I'm glad.

536
00:29:48,053 --> 00:29:50,188
It's a bit hard for me, though.

537
00:29:52,557 --> 00:29:54,993
Listen carefully to me from now on.

538
00:29:55,060 --> 00:29:56,628
I won't say it twice, got it?

539
00:29:56,695 --> 00:29:57,996
Yes, sir.

540
00:29:58,063 --> 00:29:59,998
Planting seedlings is simple.

541
00:30:00,065 --> 00:30:03,068
Anyone who isn't a total fool knows it.

542
00:30:03,135 --> 00:30:06,271
First, fill this seedling tray
with potting mix,

543
00:30:06,338 --> 00:30:09,007
not too much or too little, just right.

544
00:30:09,074 --> 00:30:11,543
Then take two cabbage seeds at a time

545
00:30:11,610 --> 00:30:14,546
and press two firmly into each hole.

546
00:30:14,613 --> 00:30:17,349
Not too deep or shallow,
just right, like this.

547
00:30:17,416 --> 00:30:19,318
He says "just right" all the time.

548
00:30:19,384 --> 00:30:20,986
If we understood "just right,"

549
00:30:21,053 --> 00:30:22,454
would we be in this mess?

550
00:30:22,521 --> 00:30:24,122
Right! Cooking shows do that.

551
00:30:24,189 --> 00:30:27,192
"Salt just right, sugar just right."
Are they kidding?

552
00:30:27,259 --> 00:30:29,227
Hey, punks! Your teacher's lecturing,

553
00:30:29,294 --> 00:30:31,229
and you keep yapping like lunatics?

554
00:30:31,296 --> 00:30:33,198
We're sorry.

555
00:30:33,265 --> 00:30:35,334
Um, Teach, I have a question.

556
00:30:35,400 --> 00:30:37,636
Why waste two or three cabbage seeds?

557
00:30:37,703 --> 00:30:39,037
Good question.

558
00:30:39,104 --> 00:30:43,275
Why do we put two or three seeds
in a hole instead of just one?

559
00:30:43,342 --> 00:30:45,811
Say you plant just one
to save cabbage seeds.

560
00:30:45,877 --> 00:30:48,080
But the seed's a dud, like you guys?

561
00:30:49,047 --> 00:30:50,515
Then it might not germinate.

562
00:30:50,582 --> 00:30:54,319
And even if they germinate,
does every single one grow well?

563
00:30:54,386 --> 00:30:55,620
Not in the least!

564
00:30:56,288 --> 00:30:58,256
Some are puny and weak like you guys,

565
00:30:58,323 --> 00:31:02,027
and some are solid and sturdy like me.

566
00:31:02,094 --> 00:31:04,563
So with puny, weak ones like you guys,

567
00:31:04,629 --> 00:31:06,098
what must we do with them?

568
00:31:07,332 --> 00:31:08,800
We eliminate them.

569
00:31:08,867 --> 00:31:11,436
The technical term is "thinning," okay?

570
00:31:11,503 --> 00:31:13,238
Go on, give it a try.

571
00:31:17,376 --> 00:31:18,410
Fill it just right.

572
00:31:18,477 --> 00:31:21,947
Hey, punk, too much potting mix!
Fill it just right! Just right!

573
00:31:22,013 --> 00:31:24,449
Just right, buddy.
Just right, like this.

574
00:31:26,585 --> 00:31:30,222
You planted them way too deep!
They won't take root like that.

575
00:31:30,288 --> 00:31:32,924
Not too deep or shallow.
Press it in just right!

576
00:31:32,991 --> 00:31:34,493
Can't you understand me?

577
00:31:34,559 --> 00:31:37,295
Jeez, stop yelling.
It's their first time.

578
00:31:37,362 --> 00:31:38,663
Were you good at first?

579
00:31:38,730 --> 00:31:40,866
I was good right from the start.

580
00:31:40,932 --> 00:31:44,102
Wait, why have you been
taking these guys' side?

581
00:31:44,803 --> 00:31:46,438
-When did I?
-Who is it?

582
00:31:46,505 --> 00:31:47,906
Who did you fall for now?

583
00:31:47,973 --> 00:31:49,541
Is it him? Or him?

584
00:31:49,608 --> 00:31:50,475
Tell me, hurry!

585
00:31:50,542 --> 00:31:52,477
I didn't fall for anyone.

586
00:31:52,544 --> 00:31:53,712
Give me a break.

587
00:31:54,980 --> 00:31:56,214
Stop right there!

588
00:31:56,281 --> 00:31:58,817
You little brat! Get back here!

589
00:31:59,951 --> 00:32:02,287
Hey, you guys, I'm warning you now.

590
00:32:02,354 --> 00:32:05,123
Don't you dare eye my sister.

591
00:32:05,190 --> 00:32:08,226
If you do, you die and I die, got it?

592
00:32:09,194 --> 00:32:10,162
I-ji!

593
00:32:10,228 --> 00:32:13,031
That little brat! Hwang I-ji!

594
00:32:13,098 --> 00:32:14,833
He could've just let it go…

595
00:32:14,900 --> 00:32:18,303
Eye her? Who's eyeing her?
Why's he acting like that, seriously?

596
00:32:18,370 --> 00:32:21,139
Even on the slim chance I liked I-ji,

597
00:32:21,206 --> 00:32:22,974
I'd never date her because of him.

598
00:32:23,041 --> 00:32:24,176
Me neither.

599
00:32:24,242 --> 00:32:26,311
Excuse me, ma'am, I have a question.

600
00:32:27,078 --> 00:32:29,614
Sang-deuk and that woman from earlier…

601
00:32:29,681 --> 00:32:31,516
It seems like there's a story.

602
00:32:31,583 --> 00:32:33,919
Who? Oh, Mi-yeong?

603
00:32:33,985 --> 00:32:34,953
Yes.

604
00:32:35,020 --> 00:32:37,022
So here's what happened.

605
00:32:37,622 --> 00:32:40,225
Forget it. You'll just say
I have a big mouth again.

606
00:32:40,292 --> 00:32:41,159
I won't tell.

607
00:32:41,226 --> 00:32:43,295
Right, why pry into others' lives?

608
00:32:43,361 --> 00:32:44,529
-Back to work.
-Okay.

609
00:32:46,131 --> 00:32:48,967
-Hey, you overfilled it.
-What now?

610
00:32:49,034 --> 00:32:51,336
-It's overflowing.
-You're messing up too.

611
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:54,439
They dated and even promised to marry.

612
00:32:55,607 --> 00:32:56,908
You said you wouldn't?

613
00:32:56,975 --> 00:32:59,644
I'm telling you so you aren't
too curious to work.

614
00:32:59,711 --> 00:33:01,980
So this is purely for your own good.

615
00:33:02,781 --> 00:33:04,483
Sang-deuk and Mi-yeong

616
00:33:04,549 --> 00:33:07,486
were the most lovey-dovey
couple in this town.

617
00:33:22,467 --> 00:33:26,438
Why? Is my playing
distracting you from studying?

618
00:33:26,505 --> 00:33:28,039
No.

619
00:33:29,307 --> 00:33:33,078
Sang-deuk, should I just marry you?

620
00:33:33,879 --> 00:33:35,780
Well, that goes without saying.

621
00:33:36,715 --> 00:33:39,918
No, I mean right after high school.

622
00:33:42,287 --> 00:33:44,356
What do you mean? Not go to college?

623
00:33:45,724 --> 00:33:48,059
It's not like I can afford college.

624
00:33:49,261 --> 00:33:51,062
I'd rather just marry you.

625
00:33:51,129 --> 00:33:53,365
What are you talking about right now?

626
00:33:53,431 --> 00:33:55,400
Don't worry about tuition. Study hard.

627
00:33:55,467 --> 00:33:57,235
I told you I'd support you fully.

628
00:33:57,302 --> 00:33:59,604
-I just feel sorry.
-Shh.

629
00:33:59,671 --> 00:34:03,375
Shh, people in love don't say sorry.

630
00:34:04,342 --> 00:34:06,211
If you're really sorry,

631
00:34:06,278 --> 00:34:08,547
just give me a kiss instead.

632
00:34:09,281 --> 00:34:10,982
A kiss?

633
00:34:12,884 --> 00:34:14,553
Oh, whatever.

634
00:34:32,170 --> 00:34:33,305
Applicant number

635
00:34:33,371 --> 00:34:36,942
21094,

636
00:34:37,008 --> 00:34:38,577
you have been accepted.

637
00:34:38,643 --> 00:34:40,211
What was that?

638
00:34:42,647 --> 00:34:44,783
Sang-deuk, I got in!

639
00:34:46,251 --> 00:34:48,453
Sang-deuk, am I dreaming? Hit me!

640
00:34:48,520 --> 00:34:50,388
How could I ever hit you…

641
00:34:52,190 --> 00:34:53,892
It's not a dream.

642
00:34:57,996 --> 00:34:58,863
You got in!

643
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:01,866
That year, Mi-yeong got into
a university in Seoul.

644
00:35:10,542 --> 00:35:11,610
Sang-deuk!

645
00:35:11,676 --> 00:35:14,946
Mi-yeong, if you're short on money
in Seoul, let me know.

646
00:35:15,013 --> 00:35:16,348
I'll call once in Seoul.

647
00:35:16,414 --> 00:35:18,283
Okay, all right. Go on.

648
00:35:18,350 --> 00:35:19,551
GEUMSEONG TRANSPORT

649
00:35:19,618 --> 00:35:20,852
-Sang-deuk.
-Mi-yeong.

650
00:35:20,919 --> 00:35:22,187
Sang-deuk.

651
00:35:22,854 --> 00:35:25,657
Mi-yeong! Take me with you!

652
00:35:25,724 --> 00:35:27,959
Let me go with you!

653
00:35:28,026 --> 00:35:29,995
Help! Save me!

654
00:35:30,061 --> 00:35:31,896
Take care and don't catch a cold.

655
00:35:31,963 --> 00:35:34,866
-Call me if you need money, okay?
-Okay, okay.

656
00:35:43,842 --> 00:35:46,177
After that, Sang-deuk
worked to the bone

657
00:35:46,244 --> 00:35:50,248
farming to pay all of Mi-yeong's
tuition, allowance, and room rent.

658
00:35:56,221 --> 00:36:00,759
On top of that, he personally brought
her side dishes with utmost devotion.

659
00:36:02,927 --> 00:36:04,829
But then, one day…

660
00:36:48,940 --> 00:36:53,111
Under Seoul's bright moon, I roamed
late into the night and returned.

661
00:36:53,178 --> 00:36:56,448
I look upon the bed and see four legs.

662
00:36:56,514 --> 00:36:57,449
SONG OF CHEOYONG

663
00:36:57,515 --> 00:37:00,852
Two of them were mine,
but whose are the other two?

664
00:37:01,453 --> 00:37:04,089
They were once mine, though.

665
00:37:04,155 --> 00:37:06,191
What can I do now that they're taken?

666
00:37:17,769 --> 00:37:20,538
Sang-deuk…

667
00:37:20,605 --> 00:37:22,707
You wicked girl.

668
00:37:22,774 --> 00:37:24,175
YOU WICKED GIRL

669
00:37:32,851 --> 00:37:34,652
So the two of them broke up.

670
00:37:34,719 --> 00:37:36,087
Once Mi-yeong graduated,

671
00:37:36,154 --> 00:37:38,356
I heard she married a rich man.

672
00:37:38,423 --> 00:37:41,960
Now that she's back like that,
no wonder his mom's hopping mad.

673
00:37:42,727 --> 00:37:45,263
That woman really crossed the line!

674
00:37:45,330 --> 00:37:47,165
-You scared me!
-So annoying, geez.

675
00:37:47,232 --> 00:37:51,035
So that's why Sang-deuk drank so much.

676
00:37:51,102 --> 00:37:53,671
No, he drank like a fish
since elementary school.

677
00:37:53,738 --> 00:37:54,873
What?

678
00:37:54,939 --> 00:37:57,275
So he just liked to drink.

679
00:37:57,342 --> 00:37:59,744
-Since his youth.
-Elementary school…

680
00:38:00,578 --> 00:38:01,513
What time is it?

681
00:38:01,579 --> 00:38:02,981
Late again means no food!

682
00:38:03,047 --> 00:38:04,048
Hurry, hurry! Run!

683
00:38:04,115 --> 00:38:06,050
-Yes, ma'am.
-I'm sorry, so sorry.

684
00:38:11,790 --> 00:38:13,124
What is this?

685
00:38:13,191 --> 00:38:15,193
They fed us only ramen every day.

686
00:38:15,260 --> 00:38:16,494
Now a canned buffet?

687
00:38:16,561 --> 00:38:18,997
I thought country meals
would be different.

688
00:38:19,063 --> 00:38:20,999
How is everything instant food?

689
00:38:21,065 --> 00:38:23,234
Whining when you don't earn your keep.

690
00:38:23,301 --> 00:38:24,836
Just eat what you're given.

691
00:38:24,903 --> 00:38:27,839
This isn't whining, this is too much.

692
00:38:27,906 --> 00:38:30,508
All right, okay.

693
00:38:30,575 --> 00:38:33,244
I'll make a tasty dinner,
so look forward to it.

694
00:38:33,311 --> 00:38:35,246
I should go grocery shopping.

695
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:37,782
-Thank you, ma'am!
-Thank you!

696
00:38:37,849 --> 00:38:39,217
Yes! Thank you!

697
00:38:39,284 --> 00:38:42,887
These punks just had to go
and open Pandora's box.

698
00:38:42,954 --> 00:38:45,190
I'll teach these rotten punks!

699
00:38:45,256 --> 00:38:47,225
Please calm down, Uncle.

700
00:38:47,292 --> 00:38:49,360
They'll have to face it once anyway.

701
00:38:49,427 --> 00:38:51,162
Well, I suppose so.

702
00:38:51,229 --> 00:38:53,865
They dug their own graves.

703
00:39:02,373 --> 00:39:03,641
What is it, Mom?

704
00:39:03,708 --> 00:39:07,245
Stay sharp and do well on your date.

705
00:39:07,312 --> 00:39:09,614
Gosh, I told you not to worry.

706
00:39:09,681 --> 00:39:12,617
You aren't still hung up
on that hussy Mi-yeong?

707
00:39:12,684 --> 00:39:14,352
I told you I'm not.

708
00:39:14,419 --> 00:39:16,921
I got over Mi-yeong ages ago.

709
00:39:17,622 --> 00:39:20,391
I'll do great this time. Don't worry.

710
00:39:20,458 --> 00:39:22,093
I'm hanging up.

711
00:39:23,361 --> 00:39:24,963
She worries over nothing.

712
00:39:25,029 --> 00:39:27,832
Am I crazy? Why care
about a woman who dumped me?

713
00:39:27,899 --> 00:39:29,601
And a divorcée, at that?

714
00:39:30,335 --> 00:39:32,470
This woman's way prettier and younger.

715
00:39:32,537 --> 00:39:34,005
Why would I?

716
00:39:34,572 --> 00:39:38,676
This time, I'll pull it off
and get married for all to see!

717
00:39:40,111 --> 00:39:41,212
Mr. Park Sang-deuk?

718
00:39:43,114 --> 00:39:45,283
Yes, I'm Park Sang-deuk…

719
00:39:49,954 --> 00:39:52,690
-Who are you?
-I'm so sorry.

720
00:39:52,757 --> 00:39:54,626
I'm pretty late, aren't I?

721
00:39:56,494 --> 00:39:58,830
I'm Lee Bong-ryeon, your blind date.

722
00:39:58,897 --> 00:40:00,231
Excuse me?

723
00:40:02,934 --> 00:40:04,435
Is there a problem?

724
00:40:04,502 --> 00:40:06,604
No, not at all.

725
00:40:07,105 --> 00:40:09,407
Goddamn Photoshop.

726
00:40:15,380 --> 00:40:20,118
You look way older than in your photo.

727
00:40:20,184 --> 00:40:22,820
Anyway, you just can't trust photos.

728
00:40:22,887 --> 00:40:25,590
I'm just kidding.

729
00:40:31,429 --> 00:40:32,397
My, why look there?

730
00:40:32,463 --> 00:40:34,465
What? What did I look at?

731
00:40:34,532 --> 00:40:36,834
You just looked at my chest.

732
00:40:36,901 --> 00:40:38,970
You're so naughty.

733
00:40:39,037 --> 00:40:43,308
Men just lose their minds
whenever they see my chest.

734
00:40:46,477 --> 00:40:48,346
Min-ho!

735
00:40:49,247 --> 00:40:52,116
It's almost dinnertime. Where'd he go?

736
00:40:54,752 --> 00:40:56,321
What's this?

737
00:41:01,893 --> 00:41:04,362
I think it was over here.

738
00:41:04,429 --> 00:41:05,463
Got it! I got it!

739
00:41:05,530 --> 00:41:07,999
Look, it's Yun-hee.

740
00:41:09,067 --> 00:41:10,268
Hey, Kang Min-ho!

741
00:41:10,335 --> 00:41:12,770
It's dinnertime.
What are you doing here?

742
00:41:12,837 --> 00:41:14,005
Min-gi, didn't I say

743
00:41:14,072 --> 00:41:15,606
you're banned from Min-ho?

744
00:41:15,673 --> 00:41:17,608
What am I, a criminal?

745
00:41:17,675 --> 00:41:19,844
Why do you always pick on just me?

746
00:41:19,911 --> 00:41:22,413
Why not come in
and do another flying kick?

747
00:41:22,480 --> 00:41:23,348
Hmph, bleh!

748
00:41:23,414 --> 00:41:26,150
What a childish jerk. Why, that…

749
00:41:26,217 --> 00:41:28,519
Don't be like that, Yun-hee. Come in.

750
00:41:28,586 --> 00:41:29,821
Forget it.

751
00:41:29,887 --> 00:41:31,756
I'm not splashing around at my age.

752
00:41:31,823 --> 00:41:33,491
Get out, or you'll catch a cold.

753
00:41:33,558 --> 00:41:35,326
Hurry home. Go on, hurry home.

754
00:41:35,393 --> 00:41:38,029
She's so dry.
What is she, semi-dried squid?

755
00:41:38,096 --> 00:41:40,565
Come on, hurry up.

756
00:41:44,802 --> 00:41:46,137
Hurry on over.

757
00:41:47,872 --> 00:41:49,207
What's with him?

758
00:41:53,044 --> 00:41:55,580
What's wrong with him? Is he crazy?

759
00:41:56,147 --> 00:41:57,315
Has he lost his mind?

760
00:41:57,382 --> 00:41:58,983
Get out of my way!

761
00:41:59,617 --> 00:42:02,053
Oh, no! Oh, no!

762
00:42:02,120 --> 00:42:04,288
Yun-hui! Yun-hui!

763
00:42:07,458 --> 00:42:08,459
Ow, ouch.

764
00:42:10,194 --> 00:42:13,064
You sprained it badly.
You should go see a doctor.

765
00:42:13,131 --> 00:42:15,533
I don't need a doctor
for something so minor.

766
00:42:15,600 --> 00:42:17,368
It'll heal if I rest a few days.

767
00:42:18,636 --> 00:42:20,571
This is all your fault, you hear?

768
00:42:20,638 --> 00:42:22,173
You stay away from me too.

769
00:42:22,240 --> 00:42:23,474
I'm sorry.

770
00:42:23,541 --> 00:42:26,878
Don't you have a delivery
to Seoul tomorrow?

771
00:42:26,944 --> 00:42:29,680
But how can you drive with that foot?

772
00:42:29,747 --> 00:42:30,915
Tell me about it.

773
00:42:30,982 --> 00:42:33,317
Going to Seoul tomorrow? I'll come too.

774
00:42:33,384 --> 00:42:34,485
What do you mean?

775
00:42:34,552 --> 00:42:36,054
No, we've got tons of work.

776
00:42:36,120 --> 00:42:39,157
I have something important.
Cut me some slack tomorrow.

777
00:42:39,223 --> 00:42:40,725
That works out well.

778
00:42:40,792 --> 00:42:44,262
Then it'd be great
if you drove for Yun-hui.

779
00:42:44,328 --> 00:42:45,863
-Drive?
-Yes.

780
00:42:45,930 --> 00:42:47,432
I do have a license, but

781
00:42:47,498 --> 00:42:49,333
I've never driven since I got it…

782
00:42:49,400 --> 00:42:51,803
If you insist, I'll give it a try.

783
00:42:51,869 --> 00:42:53,738
Hitting the gas stops it, right?

784
00:42:53,805 --> 00:42:55,106
Gosh, hey, forget it!

785
00:42:55,173 --> 00:42:56,174
Don't do anything.

786
00:42:56,240 --> 00:42:57,442
You'll kill someone!

787
00:42:57,508 --> 00:42:58,843
Uncle, this guy here

788
00:42:58,910 --> 00:43:00,144
is only big and tall,

789
00:43:00,211 --> 00:43:01,813
but can't do a single thing.

790
00:43:01,879 --> 00:43:03,381
It'd be a disaster. No, no.

791
00:43:03,448 --> 00:43:06,951
Then does anyone else have a license?

792
00:43:09,320 --> 00:43:12,390
I do have one, but isn't it a truck?

793
00:43:12,457 --> 00:43:14,292
I only have a Class 2 license.

794
00:43:14,358 --> 00:43:16,194
Mine is Class 2 as well.

795
00:43:17,061 --> 00:43:19,864
-Min-gi has a Class 1 license.
-Yes, that's right!

796
00:43:19,931 --> 00:43:24,235
Is that so? Then it'd be great
if you drove tomorrow.

797
00:43:24,302 --> 00:43:26,704
-Why me?
-She got hurt because of you.

798
00:43:27,438 --> 00:43:30,408
If you'd rather not,
I'd gladly do the same to your foot.

799
00:43:30,475 --> 00:43:33,711
All right, all right! I'll go.

800
00:43:34,345 --> 00:43:36,080
We leave early at dawn tomorrow.

801
00:43:36,147 --> 00:43:37,849
Be out right on time, got it?

802
00:43:37,915 --> 00:43:39,317
Got it.

803
00:43:45,656 --> 00:43:46,858
What brings you here?

804
00:43:47,859 --> 00:43:49,060
I'm not here for you.

805
00:43:51,762 --> 00:43:54,999
Hello, my dear sir.

806
00:43:57,335 --> 00:43:59,804
Oh, hi there.

807
00:44:00,304 --> 00:44:02,807
Hey, are you playing favorites?

808
00:44:02,874 --> 00:44:05,843
You call me "you,"
so why is Hyeok "my dear sir"?

809
00:44:07,078 --> 00:44:10,114
It's my own tongue.
Can't I talk however I want?

810
00:44:11,382 --> 00:44:12,884
Sir?

811
00:44:14,252 --> 00:44:17,522
Isn't that right, my dear sir?

812
00:44:20,625 --> 00:44:22,393
Anyway, why did you come here?

813
00:44:23,594 --> 00:44:25,930
Your wife told me to come for dinner.

814
00:44:25,997 --> 00:44:27,999
What? Dinner?

815
00:44:29,400 --> 00:44:31,469
Oh, damn it.

816
00:44:38,576 --> 00:44:40,811
So what kind of stew is this?

817
00:44:40,878 --> 00:44:43,247
It's carbonara mozzarella kimchi stew.

818
00:44:43,881 --> 00:44:46,150
Carbonara?

819
00:44:46,951 --> 00:44:49,086
-Mozzarella?
-Kimchi stew?

820
00:44:49,153 --> 00:44:52,089
Plain kimchi stew is boring, you know.

821
00:44:52,156 --> 00:44:54,225
I'm quite fond of fusion cuisine.

822
00:44:54,292 --> 00:44:57,328
Plus, since you're all from Seoul,

823
00:44:57,395 --> 00:44:59,063
I thought it'd suit your taste,

824
00:44:59,130 --> 00:45:01,666
so I showed off my cooking skills.

825
00:45:01,732 --> 00:45:03,434
What are you doing? Please eat.

826
00:45:03,501 --> 00:45:04,936
-Yes.
-Thanks for the food.

827
00:45:05,002 --> 00:45:06,604
-Elders first.
-No, no, eat.

828
00:45:06,671 --> 00:45:08,739
Thanks for the food.

829
00:45:20,318 --> 00:45:22,887
What? Why? What's wrong?

830
00:45:22,954 --> 00:45:24,455
Does it taste bad?

831
00:45:24,522 --> 00:45:27,592
This taste is just indescribable.

832
00:45:27,658 --> 00:45:31,262
It's like drinking dirty dishwater?

833
00:45:32,830 --> 00:45:34,632
Dirty dishwater?

834
00:45:36,267 --> 00:45:37,935
Is my cooking really that bad?

835
00:45:38,002 --> 00:45:41,205
Yes, this isn't fit for humans to eat.

836
00:45:41,272 --> 00:45:43,341
You really are a terrible cook.

837
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:45,276
What did you say?

838
00:45:45,343 --> 00:45:48,579
I've never once heard that before.

839
00:45:53,351 --> 00:45:54,986
Don't tell me…

840
00:45:55,586 --> 00:45:59,023
is that why you and the kids

841
00:45:59,590 --> 00:46:02,893
always asked me to just make ramen?

842
00:46:02,960 --> 00:46:04,862
Is that true?

843
00:46:04,929 --> 00:46:06,731
No, honey, darling.

844
00:46:06,797 --> 00:46:10,434
It's not that it tastes bad, exactly.

845
00:46:10,501 --> 00:46:13,371
Your experimental spirit is just

846
00:46:13,437 --> 00:46:16,173
way too unconventional, I guess, so…

847
00:46:16,240 --> 00:46:19,910
I see. So that's what it was.

848
00:46:20,678 --> 00:46:23,180
I was the only one who didn't know.

849
00:46:24,915 --> 00:46:26,684
Oh my, I'm so sorry.

850
00:46:26,751 --> 00:46:28,886
I'm truly sorry.

851
00:46:28,953 --> 00:46:30,955
Wait, honey… Darling, oh, no!

852
00:46:31,522 --> 00:46:32,590
Darn it.

853
00:46:32,657 --> 00:46:34,692
What are you guys going to do now?

854
00:46:34,759 --> 00:46:38,663
I griped about food as a newlywed,
and she cried for a month and a half!

855
00:46:38,729 --> 00:46:41,899
You guys fix this! Fix this, you punks!

856
00:46:41,966 --> 00:46:44,001
Honey! Honey!

857
00:46:44,068 --> 00:46:47,471
Boy, the mood around the house
will be gloomy again for a while.

858
00:46:48,939 --> 00:46:50,508
Try watching your mouths.

859
00:46:50,574 --> 00:46:53,644
Last time I said she had more wrinkles,
I didn't see her

860
00:46:54,412 --> 00:46:55,613
for two months.

861
00:47:03,220 --> 00:47:04,622
Hey, Sang-deuk!

862
00:47:04,689 --> 00:47:06,490
How did it go? How was it?

863
00:47:06,557 --> 00:47:08,192
It was a total bust. A bust.

864
00:47:08,259 --> 00:47:10,161
She looked nothing like her photo.

865
00:47:10,227 --> 00:47:13,264
She used Photoshop to add height
and puff up her chest.

866
00:47:13,331 --> 00:47:14,665
It was quite a sight.

867
00:47:14,732 --> 00:47:16,834
Can you live on good looks forever?

868
00:47:16,901 --> 00:47:19,003
If that were all, I wouldn't complain.

869
00:47:19,603 --> 00:47:21,605
She snorts like a pig when she laughs!

870
00:47:24,141 --> 00:47:27,111
Plus, she has the rudest
princess complex I've ever seen.

871
00:47:27,178 --> 00:47:29,814
I didn't look.
She covered her chest and skirt.

872
00:47:30,481 --> 00:47:31,749
So repulsive, really.

873
00:47:31,816 --> 00:47:34,151
Hey, still, she says she likes you.

874
00:47:34,218 --> 00:47:37,355
-Just meet her one more time.
-Forget it.

875
00:47:37,421 --> 00:47:39,890
I'd rather stay single my whole life.

876
00:47:39,957 --> 00:47:40,991
She's not the one.

877
00:47:41,058 --> 00:47:42,660
Is it Mi-yeong? Be honest.

878
00:47:42,727 --> 00:47:44,161
What nonsense is that?

879
00:47:44,228 --> 00:47:46,764
I just really didn't like that woman!

880
00:47:46,831 --> 00:47:48,532
That bitch Mi-yeong, today I'll…

881
00:47:48,599 --> 00:47:49,567
Where to, Mom?

882
00:47:50,634 --> 00:47:52,470
I'm losing my mind, seriously.

883
00:47:52,536 --> 00:47:53,571
Mom!

884
00:47:54,939 --> 00:47:57,041
Mi-yeong, you get out here!

885
00:47:57,108 --> 00:47:58,509
Come out here right now!

886
00:48:00,111 --> 00:48:01,379
Ma'am?

887
00:48:02,646 --> 00:48:04,014
Ma'am…

888
00:48:04,749 --> 00:48:06,650
-What brings you here?
-Well.

889
00:48:06,717 --> 00:48:09,687
Because of you, Sang-deuk
refuses to see his blind date.

890
00:48:09,754 --> 00:48:13,657
Who are you to suddenly come down here
and stir up Sang-deuk's feelings?

891
00:48:14,458 --> 00:48:16,227
Um, what do you mean…

892
00:48:16,894 --> 00:48:18,729
Mom, what are you talking about?

893
00:48:18,796 --> 00:48:21,532
Sang-deuk, is that true?
Was it because of me?

894
00:48:21,599 --> 00:48:23,000
That's not it at all.

895
00:48:23,667 --> 00:48:25,770
I really just didn't like that woman!

896
00:48:25,836 --> 00:48:27,671
Don't lie to me, you brat!

897
00:48:27,738 --> 00:48:30,141
Please stop it, Mom!

898
00:48:30,207 --> 00:48:32,109
I'll see her! I'll see her, okay?

899
00:48:32,176 --> 00:48:35,846
I'll call her right now and see her
again tomorrow. Will that do?

900
00:48:35,913 --> 00:48:37,648
-You mean it?
-I said I will.

901
00:48:37,715 --> 00:48:39,950
So come on, let's go quickly.

902
00:48:40,017 --> 00:48:41,819
I'm so humiliated, seriously.

903
00:48:42,620 --> 00:48:44,955
-Why are you doing that?
-Oh, honestly.

904
00:48:47,191 --> 00:48:49,226
Someone like me isn't worth it.

905
00:48:55,099 --> 00:48:56,867
You're wearing sweats to Seoul?

906
00:48:56,934 --> 00:48:58,669
I don't have any clothes, jeez.

907
00:49:00,037 --> 00:49:02,573
How long is she going to keep that up?

908
00:49:02,640 --> 00:49:05,142
She cried all last night,
so I barely slept.

909
00:49:05,209 --> 00:49:07,278
Shut up, you little punks!

910
00:49:07,344 --> 00:49:08,813
Your room's across the hall.

911
00:49:08,879 --> 00:49:11,682
Right next to her,
I didn't sleep a wink all night!

912
00:49:11,749 --> 00:49:14,985
This is all your fault, you punks!

913
00:49:16,020 --> 00:49:18,022
Honey.

914
00:49:18,088 --> 00:49:20,024
Bring me some water.

915
00:49:20,090 --> 00:49:22,193
Mix some vitamins in it.

916
00:49:23,260 --> 00:49:25,396
Okay, I'll bring it right in.

917
00:49:25,463 --> 00:49:26,931
Hey, off you go.

918
00:49:26,997 --> 00:49:28,399
Those little punks.

919
00:49:32,837 --> 00:49:36,841
She said we were late,
so why isn't she coming out?

920
00:49:36,907 --> 00:49:38,576
-She always dawdles.
-She's here.

921
00:49:38,642 --> 00:49:39,643
Hello.

922
00:49:39,710 --> 00:49:42,112
-You're here.
-Hurry, let's go, let's go!

923
00:49:42,179 --> 00:49:43,280
Hold on.

924
00:49:44,248 --> 00:49:46,217
You'd wear this tacky thing to Seoul?

925
00:49:50,888 --> 00:49:52,189
Who cares if it's tacky?

926
00:49:52,256 --> 00:49:53,958
Keeping the money safe is best.

927
00:49:54,024 --> 00:49:55,659
I'm the one who's humiliated!

928
00:49:55,726 --> 00:49:58,028
Enough, shut up. You just drive right.

929
00:49:58,095 --> 00:49:59,096
Go, go! Hurry up!

930
00:49:59,163 --> 00:50:00,898
Here, I'll help you.

931
00:50:00,965 --> 00:50:03,801
It's fine. I can handle it on my own.

932
00:50:08,839 --> 00:50:11,175
-See you!
-Have a safe trip.

933
00:50:12,543 --> 00:50:13,978
Let's head inside.

934
00:50:26,023 --> 00:50:28,125
How long will you keep this up?

935
00:50:28,192 --> 00:50:29,527
You'll just pine away?

936
00:50:29,593 --> 00:50:32,530
Your image is fixed, so just confess.

937
00:50:32,596 --> 00:50:33,831
Confess?

938
00:50:37,368 --> 00:50:40,170
Min-gi, you make sure to drive safely.

939
00:50:40,237 --> 00:50:42,206
I'll just listen to some music.

940
00:50:43,908 --> 00:50:47,144
-What song is it?
-Take a listen.

941
00:50:49,446 --> 00:50:52,182
YOON HYE-RIM VOL. 1

942
00:50:53,284 --> 00:50:55,252
What is this lousy song?

943
00:50:55,319 --> 00:50:58,088
What is this, the 1980s?
Play something else!

944
00:50:58,155 --> 00:51:01,058
Leave it alone unless you want to die.

945
00:51:09,633 --> 00:51:12,036
Hey, why do you want to get off here?

946
00:51:12,102 --> 00:51:13,437
Date with my girlfriend.

947
00:51:13,504 --> 00:51:15,873
Girlfriend? Didn't you say she died?

948
00:51:15,940 --> 00:51:18,275
-You have a girlfriend?
-Yes. Think I'm you?

949
00:51:19,677 --> 00:51:21,979
Anyway, I'll call you after my date.

950
00:51:23,180 --> 00:51:25,249
Oh, could you lend me some money?

951
00:51:25,316 --> 00:51:26,483
What?

952
00:51:26,550 --> 00:51:29,320
I'm seeing my girlfriend.
I should bring her flowers.

953
00:51:29,386 --> 00:51:33,490
Oh, no! Goodness! Oh, goodness, no!

954
00:51:34,458 --> 00:51:36,760
I'll pay you back with interest.

955
00:51:38,996 --> 00:51:42,333
Hey, what's wrong with your friend?
He's a total nutjob.

956
00:51:42,399 --> 00:51:44,468
Seriously, that little bastard…

957
00:51:44,535 --> 00:51:46,437
What a thieving little punk!

958
00:51:46,503 --> 00:51:49,039
You're just as bad as he is.

959
00:51:49,106 --> 00:51:51,308
-He's the worst nutjob of all.
-Forget it.

960
00:51:51,375 --> 00:51:53,077
Let's go, let's go.

961
00:51:53,143 --> 00:51:55,946
HADUROK-RI SPINACH

962
00:51:56,013 --> 00:51:57,781
How have you been, sir?

963
00:51:57,848 --> 00:51:58,816
CRISPY BBQ BULGOGI

964
00:51:58,882 --> 00:52:00,751
How is it, sir? Looks good, right?

965
00:52:00,818 --> 00:52:04,054
Well, the quality's not like before…

966
00:52:04,121 --> 00:52:06,857
A few spots like these
are normal when it's organic.

967
00:52:06,924 --> 00:52:08,559
Come on, you know that, sir.

968
00:52:08,626 --> 00:52:10,227
Should I bring the boxes in?

969
00:52:10,294 --> 00:52:11,729
Oh, wait!

970
00:52:12,663 --> 00:52:14,632
Well, the thing is…

971
00:52:15,399 --> 00:52:18,035
-What is it?
-Well, you see, um…

972
00:52:21,271 --> 00:52:23,774
Boss, where do I put
the onions and spinach?

973
00:52:25,909 --> 00:52:27,378
Take it to storage, storage!

974
00:52:30,814 --> 00:52:33,350
Don't tell me you got a new supplier?

975
00:52:34,718 --> 00:52:37,154
You know times are tough for everyone.

976
00:52:37,221 --> 00:52:40,257
Yours is organic, so it's too pricey…

977
00:52:40,324 --> 00:52:41,959
I was going to call you…

978
00:52:42,026 --> 00:52:44,328
It slipped my mind. Sorry, okay?

979
00:52:44,395 --> 00:52:47,064
You said you only use organic, right?

980
00:52:47,131 --> 00:52:49,033
Didn't you swear on your conscience?

981
00:52:49,099 --> 00:52:51,335
Business is just too tough right now.

982
00:52:51,402 --> 00:52:52,836
I'll buy again when I can.

983
00:52:52,903 --> 00:52:54,038
No, thanks.

984
00:52:54,104 --> 00:52:56,540
Never call me again.
I'm done supplying you.

985
00:52:58,776 --> 00:52:59,877
ECO-FRIENDLY ONLY

986
00:52:59,943 --> 00:53:03,347
Then shouldn't you take down
that eco-friendly sign now?

987
00:53:05,482 --> 00:53:07,051
Let's go, Min-gi.

988
00:53:16,060 --> 00:53:17,828
What a rotten jerk…

989
00:53:17,895 --> 00:53:19,363
He could've called ahead…

990
00:53:19,430 --> 00:53:21,965
It'll wilt if we go back.
I'll have to toss it…

991
00:53:22,032 --> 00:53:23,734
This is a disaster…

992
00:53:23,801 --> 00:53:25,769
-Toss it?
-Right.

993
00:53:27,438 --> 00:53:28,872
Should I sell it for you?

994
00:53:28,939 --> 00:53:30,941
You? How would you do that?

995
00:53:31,608 --> 00:53:33,510
I have my ways.

996
00:53:33,577 --> 00:53:35,946
But we split the money fifty-fifty.

997
00:53:36,013 --> 00:53:39,016
Fifty-fifty? Hey, that's a bit much…

998
00:53:39,683 --> 00:53:41,318
Fine, take it or leave it.

999
00:53:41,385 --> 00:53:43,454
All right, all right.

1000
00:53:43,520 --> 00:53:45,789
I don't know how you'll sell it…

1001
00:53:45,856 --> 00:53:47,524
Fifty-fifty, deal.

1002
00:54:00,404 --> 00:54:03,674
Confess? Confess to her…

1003
00:54:03,741 --> 00:54:07,211
I don't have much time left.
Should I just go ahead and confess?

1004
00:54:08,345 --> 00:54:10,614
But should a dying guy really confess?

1005
00:54:10,681 --> 00:54:12,282
Isn't that too selfish of me?

1006
00:54:13,117 --> 00:54:16,420
Right, this is wrong. Of course not…

1007
00:54:17,221 --> 00:54:18,455
Wait, hold on!

1008
00:54:18,522 --> 00:54:20,591
I'm dying soon. Can't I be selfish?

1009
00:54:21,525 --> 00:54:24,428
Dying so young is unfair enough.
Can't I even confess?

1010
00:54:24,495 --> 00:54:27,765
Confess. Humans are selfish by nature.

1011
00:54:29,433 --> 00:54:30,634
Ki-jun!

1012
00:54:31,602 --> 00:54:33,871
-Hey, I'm stepping out.
-Where to?

1013
00:54:33,937 --> 00:54:36,240
I'm not telling you. Know why?

1014
00:54:36,306 --> 00:54:38,075
Because I'm selfish!

1015
00:54:41,979 --> 00:54:43,680
I have to do this all by…

1016
00:54:44,348 --> 00:54:46,150
Seriously, jeez.

1017
00:54:47,384 --> 00:54:49,219
When will I ever finish this?

1018
00:54:52,623 --> 00:54:55,359
Forget it, I'm taking a break, jeez.

1019
00:54:56,593 --> 00:54:59,329
Do these guys intend to farm or not?

1020
00:54:59,396 --> 00:55:01,632
They're always running off, seriously.

1021
00:55:10,874 --> 00:55:12,476
-Hold still now, okay?
-What?

1022
00:55:20,517 --> 00:55:22,085
Why? What is it this time?

1023
00:55:22,152 --> 00:55:24,354
The lady said to bring mixed noodles.

1024
00:55:24,421 --> 00:55:26,857
No, thanks. Just take that and go now.

1025
00:55:26,924 --> 00:55:28,826
They'll get soggy and be ruined.

1026
00:55:28,892 --> 00:55:30,961
-Please just eat--
-Go away! Stay back!

1027
00:55:39,736 --> 00:55:41,171
Is nothing the matter?

1028
00:55:41,238 --> 00:55:44,074
Nothing the matter?
Plenty is the matter right now!

1029
00:55:45,242 --> 00:55:47,611
Hello! Somebody save me!

1030
00:55:47,678 --> 00:55:49,313
I can't believe this.

1031
00:55:49,379 --> 00:55:51,481
LIVE ROCK CLUB

1032
00:55:59,690 --> 00:56:02,459
Hey, what happened to you?

1033
00:56:02,526 --> 00:56:04,661
What is this shabby getup?

1034
00:56:04,728 --> 00:56:06,730
And what's with the spinach? Spinach?

1035
00:56:06,797 --> 00:56:09,867
Don't ask, man. I have my reasons.

1036
00:56:09,933 --> 00:56:11,568
Reasons? Gosh, come on.

1037
00:56:12,336 --> 00:56:14,271
-Where do I put it?
-In the kitchen.

1038
00:56:14,838 --> 00:56:17,708
And keep this a secret
from the guys I know, okay?

1039
00:56:17,774 --> 00:56:19,509
Go, go, go! Hurry up.

1040
00:56:24,014 --> 00:56:26,450
Wow, this is a really nice place.

1041
00:56:26,516 --> 00:56:28,919
People must perform up there and all.

1042
00:56:29,853 --> 00:56:31,054
So many photos, too.

1043
00:56:32,489 --> 00:56:34,892
Oh, my! Isn't that Min-gi?

1044
00:56:34,958 --> 00:56:36,627
And that one is Hyeok.

1045
00:56:36,693 --> 00:56:39,730
It really is them, those dorks.

1046
00:56:39,796 --> 00:56:42,733
They were hugely popular back then.

1047
00:56:42,799 --> 00:56:46,036
I bet. Dressed like that,
